<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani yarn rates end steady, seen rising.</title>
<headline>Pakistani yarn rates end steady, seen rising.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani cotton yarn rates closed steady on Wednesday but dealers said that they would rise following increases in domestic cotton rates.</p>
<p>They said higher export demand for yarn was also likely to push rates up. Rates in rupees supplied by the Pakistan Yarn Merchant Association for a 10-lb (4.54 kg) cone of 21 counts:</p>
<p>				     Wednesday    Previous</p>
<p>    Al-Karam (A.K.)	    500	    500</p>
<p>    Globe (Hina)		 500	    500</p>
<p>    M.G.M.			 490	    490</p>
<p>    ($1 = 40.22 rupees)    -- Ovais Subhani 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
